message: "If you use this code or its derived tables, please cite it as below. Cite IMF PortWatch for the underlying data."
title: "AUDIT #1: Strait of Hormuz, IMF PortWatch tanker mass balance"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tranquilli
    given-names: Alberto
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - IMF PortWatch
  - AIS
  - Strait of Hormuz
  - data quality
  - GNSS interference
abstract: >-
  Internal consistency check between IMF PortWatch's port and chokepoint tanker series at the Strait of
  Hormuz, 1 Mar to 25 Sep 2026. One terminal with implausible port-call bursts accounts for about half of a
  10.23 Mt gap. The license covers the code only, not PortWatch data.
references:
  - type: data
    title: "IMF PortWatch: Daily Port Activity and Trade Estimates; Daily Chokepoint Transit Calls and Trade Volume Estimates"
    authors:
      - name: "International Monetary Fund, PortWatch (sources: Kpler; UN Global Platform)"
    url: "https://portwatch.imf.org"
